{
  "uid": "apps-v2-authz-service-overview",
  "title": "Authz Service — Overview",
  "description": "Authorization answers for nxmain, the nx-pipeline API and the UI: whether a user may query a datasource, which fields they see, which datasources they can list or guard, and the grant and credential management behind them. The service instruments one thing, every RPC, with the shared gRPC set from pipeline-lib (grpc_requests_total, grpc_request_duration_seconds, grpc_active_requests) over its Connect handler: it serves Connect over HTTP, but the interceptor records each call as an RPC, so there are no http_* series. There are no domain metrics. With METRICS_ENABLED=false only the Go and process collectors are served and every RPC panel is empty.",
  "folderUid": "apps-v2-authz-service-folder",
  "tags": [
    "git-sync",
    "apps-v2",
    "service:authz-service",
    "overview"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "editable": null,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "links": [
