  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 100,
      "title": "Service Health",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Pods Up",
      "description": "Pods scraped. The UI manages datasource grants and credentials through this service. nxmain and the nx-pipeline API also ask it whether a user may query a datasource, which fields they see and which datasources they can list, but only when their client.mode is authz-service; in local mode they keep their own checks and never call it. With every pod down, callers in authz-service mode fall back to their own checks, which do not know the datasources this service owns, and the UI's grant and credential screens fail outright.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(up{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"})"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Pods Ready",
      "description": "Pods passing /readyz, from kube-state-metrics. Readiness checks every dependency the pod was configured with: nx-backend's database, the JWKS, and, when set, nx-pipeline's database and this service's own. A pod Up here but not Ready is running and scraped while the Service sends it nothing: the readiness log line names the failing check. Not filtered by Pod: that list only holds pods that have been scraped, which would hide exactly the pod stuck in its migrations init container or crashlooping before /metrics.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(kube_pod_status_ready{namespace=\"$namespace\", pod=~\".*-authz-service-.*\", condition=\"true\"})"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "RPC Rate (5m)",
      "description": "RPCs per second across all of AuthzService, refused calls included. Every RPC is unary and served over Connect, and the metrics interceptor runs before the token check, so a call refused for its token is counted too. Probes and scrapes are not RPCs and are not in it. With callers in client.mode local, nothing from the query path arrives and this is UI traffic alone, so a near-zero rate is configuration, not an outage.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 2
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m]))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Server Faults % (5m)",
      "description": "Share of RPCs that failed on this side: Unknown, DeadlineExceeded, ResourceExhausted, Internal, Unavailable or DataLoss. Unavailable is the common one, and it has two causes that look alike here: a dependency down (a database, auth-service, the credential manager), and a dependency not configured at all. Without NX_PIPELINE_DB_NAME, AUTHZ_DB_NAME or the credential manager, the RPCs that need them answer Unavailable on every call, so a steady non-zero floor since a rollout is configuration; Errors by RPC & Code says which RPCs.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.01
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 2
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code=~\"$fault_codes\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])), 0.0001)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Auth Refusals % (5m)",
      "description": "Share of RPCs refused as Unauthenticated (no token or API key, or one that failed verification) or PermissionDenied (an unknown or inactive user, or a caller not allowed the RPC). Kept apart from faults because some is normal. A sudden wall of Unauthenticated across every RPC is the JWKS or the API key, not callers: check Pods Ready, which drops with the JWKS. A denial is not an error. CanQuery, HasPermission and IsDatasourceMember answer a refused caller with allowed=false and code 0, so a user being told no counts as OK everywhere on this board.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.05
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.25
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 2
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code=~\"7|16\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])), 0.0001)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "RPC p95 (5m)",
      "description": "95th-percentile RPC duration. In client.mode authz-service, nxmain and the nx-pipeline API bound each call at client.timeoutSeconds (2s in the chart) and fall back to their own checks when it fails, so a tail approaching 2s means callers are quietly answering for themselves, not that users are waiting longer. In local mode there is no caller timeout or fallback: the only callers are the UI, and a slow tail is users waiting. Empty while no RPC arrives in the window.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 20,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1.5
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 3
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(grpc_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 200,
      "title": "RPCs — Requests",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request Rate by RPC",
      "description": "One series per RPC. The method label is the Connect procedure, and only procedures in the proto reach the interceptor (an unknown path is a 404 from the mux), so the series count is bounded by the 22 RPCs. With callers in client.mode authz-service, expect CanQuery, GetFieldPolicy and GetPrincipal to dominate: nxmain and the nx-pipeline API ask them on the query path. In local mode they never call, so only the UI's datasource-management and credential RPCs appear, and those are rare.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "label_replace(sum by (method) (rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])), \"rpc\", \"$1\", \"method\", \"$rpc_regex\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{rpc}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
