    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Duration p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "Trustworthy percentiles: the service passes SubsecondLatencyBuckets to the gRPC set explicitly, so the ladder runs 0.005s to 10s rather than the OTel SDK default tuned for milliseconds. In client.mode authz-service, nxmain and the nx-pipeline API bound each call at client.timeoutSeconds (2s in the chart) and fall back to their own checks when it fails, so a tail approaching 2s means callers are quietly answering for themselves, not that users are waiting longer. In local mode there is no caller timeout or fallback: the only callers are the UI, and a slow tail is users waiting.\n\nA call that never returns is never observed, because the histogram records on return, so it moves nothing here: it shows only on RPCs In Flight.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(grpc_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(grpc_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(grpc_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Duration p95 by RPC",
      "description": "Which RPC is slow. The query-path RPCs read nx-backend's and nx-pipeline's databases; the credential RPCs call the credential manager, bounded by CREDENTIAL_MANAGER_TIMEOUT, so they sit on a different timescale and should not be read against CanQuery.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "label_replace(histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, method) (rate(grpc_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m]))), \"rpc\", \"$1\", \"method\", \"$rpc_regex\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{rpc}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Error Ratio (non-OK)",
      "description": "Share of RPCs answered with any non-OK code, with the server-fault share as a second line. The gap between them is callers being refused or rejected, which Errors by Class splits out. clamp_min keeps both ratios defined while the service is idle.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 14
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code!=\"0\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])), 0.0001)",
          "legendFormat": "non-OK"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code=~\"$fault_codes\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])), 0.0001)",
          "legendFormat": "server faults"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RPCs In Flight",
      "description": "RPCs being handled right now, by RPC. Calls take milliseconds, so a 30s scrape reads 0 almost always, and that is correct. What this catches is a call that never returns, which no other panel can show: a value that climbs and does not come back down, usually a database or the credential manager holding a connection open.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 14
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "label_replace(sum by (method) (grpc_active_requests{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}), \"rpc\", \"$1\", \"method\", \"$rpc_regex\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{rpc}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 300,
      "title": "RPCs — Errors",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Errors by RPC & Code (rate)",
      "description": "Which RPC is failing, and how. Codes: 1 Canceled, 2 Unknown, 3 InvalidArgument, 4 DeadlineExceeded, 5 NotFound, 6 AlreadyExists, 7 PermissionDenied, 8 ResourceExhausted, 9 FailedPrecondition, 10 Aborted, 11 OutOfRange, 12 Unimplemented, 13 Internal, 14 Unavailable, 15 DataLoss, 16 Unauthenticated. 2 is any error that is not a Connect error, so an unexpected failure usually lands there. A single RPC at a steady 14 since a rollout is a dependency it needs that is not configured; every RPC at 16 at once is token verification.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "label_replace(sum by (method, code) (rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code!=\"0\"}[5m])), \"rpc\", \"$1\", \"method\", \"$rpc_regex\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{rpc}} {{code}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Error Ratio by RPC (non-OK)",
      "description": "Error Ratio split by RPC. Read it with the rate beside it: the UI's RPCs are called a handful of times, so one refused call is a large share. A high ratio on a tiny rate is a single refusal, not an outage. An RPC with no errors in the window draws no line.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 23
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "label_replace(sum by (method) (rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code!=\"0\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum by (method) (rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])), 0.0001), \"rpc\", \"$1\", \"method\", \"$rpc_regex\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{rpc}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Errors by Class",
      "description": "Non-OK split three ways. Auth refusals are the caller's identity: no or bad token, an unknown or inactive user, or a caller not allowed the RPC. Rejected requests are the request itself: bad arguments, a missing datasource or credential, a write that conflicts, or the caller giving up (Canceled, which is what a caller's own timeout looks like from here). Server faults are this service or what it depends on.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code=~\"7|16\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "auth refusals (7, 16)"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code=~\"1|3|5|6|9|10|11|12\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "rejected requests (1, 3, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12)"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "sum(rate(grpc_requests_total{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", code=~\"$fault_codes\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "server faults (2, 4, 8, 13, 14, 15)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Pods Ready vs Pods Up",
      "description": "The two lines diverging is a pod running and scraped but out of the Service, because /readyz is failing on one of its dependencies. Readiness is not liveness: such a pod is not restarted, it just stops receiving calls, so a gap that persists is a dependency that stays down. Not filtered by Pod: that list only holds pods that have been scraped, which would hide exactly the pod stuck in its migrations init container or crashlooping before /metrics.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 31
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(kube_pod_status_ready{namespace=\"$namespace\", pod=~\".*-authz-service-.*\", condition=\"true\"})",
          "legendFormat": "ready"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(up{job=~\".*authz-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"})",
          "legendFormat": "up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 500,
      "title": "Per-Pod Drill-Down",
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 40,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "RPC Rate by Pod",
          "description": "Which replicas callers are reaching. A pod that is up but receiving nothing is out of the Service, usually not Ready.",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 6,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 40
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "reqps",
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 1,
                "fillOpacity": 8,
                "showPoints": "never"
              }
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "legend": {
